==================================================
1. AUDIT ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLES
==================================================

Audit history must represent historical truth.

Normal business users must not be able to:

- edit audit events
- delete audit events
- rewrite audit actor
- rewrite original timestamp
- remove approval history
- secretly remove failed attempts

Corrections must create NEW audit events.

Example:

Event 1001
Student Registered Email Changed

Event 1012
Student Registered Email Corrected

Event 1001 remains historically visible.

Design the audit architecture as append-oriented / immutable to ordinary application workflows.

Do not claim cryptographic immutability unless an actual mechanism will later implement it.

